-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLACEHOLDER — A LICENSING DECISION IS STILL OUTSTANDING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is an intentionally restrictive placeholder. No license has been chosen
for sha256 yet, and this file grants no rights to anyone other than the
copyright holder.

It is deliberately restrictive rather than permissive: granting rights is an
easy change to make later, whereas a permissive license that has already been
published cannot be meaningfully withdrawn from copies already distributed.

Before replacing this file, note that the choice is constrained by the
third-party components sha256 ends up depending on. In particular:

  * PySide6 is available under LGPL-3.0 or a commercial Qt license. LGPL
    imposes relinking obligations on distributed binaries.
  * pyvirtualcam is GPL-2.0. Linking it into a distributed application has
    copyleft consequences for the whole work.
  * Several candidate AI components license their source code and their
    pretrained weights under different terms, and some weights are restricted
    to non-commercial research use.

These are analysed in docs/OPEN_SOURCE_EVALUATION.md, and the licensing
implications of each are recorded in docs/decisions/.

Do not assume any particular outcome from this file. Until it is replaced, treat
sha256 as unlicensed proprietary software.
